+/*
+ * Device release number, reported as bcdDevice.
+ *
+ * This must not stay at 0x0000, the value this firmware used to report.
+ * Windows caches the answer to "does this device have MS OS descriptors?" in
+ * HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\usbflags\<VID><PID><bcdDevice>, and it
+ * does not ask again for a device that once said no. A host that has already
+ * seen a firmware without working MS OS descriptors would therefore never pick
+ * up the ones added here.
+ *
+ * Bumping this makes the cache key different, so the host asks afresh.
+ *
+ * Two values are deliberately avoided: 0x2608 belongs to the CANable 2.5
+ * firmware, and 0x0100 is what our patched candleLight_fw build reports on the
+ * SH-C30A. All three share VID:PID 1d50:606f, so reusing a value would give
+ * two different products the same hardware ID -- and would make one product's
+ * poisoned usbflags entry affect the other.
+ *
+ * From v1.5 on the low byte carries the version as well: the high byte stays the
+ * product line (0x02 = SH-C31x), the low byte is the BCD firmware version, so
+ * a host tells the releases apart without opening the device. 0x0200 stays v1.4.
